## Key system

```lua
local Window = Lumen:CreateWindow({
Name = "My Hub",
KeySystem = true,
KeySettings = {
Title = "My Hub",
Subtitle = "Key System",
Note = "Join our Discord to get a key.",
Key = { "KEY-1", "KEY-2" }, -- accepted keys
SaveKey = true,             -- remember a valid key between sessions
FileName = "key",
Link = "https://example.com/get-key", -- optional: adds a Get Key button that copies this
},
})
```

`CreateWindow` waits until a valid key is entered, so the code after it only runs for valid users.

> **Security note:** a key list stored inside a client script is visible to anyone who reads the script. For anything that matters, validate keys on a server (for example with a key-service provider) inside your own `Callback`/script logic.

## Configuration saving

Config saving needs an executor with file functions (`writefile`, `readfile` and so on). Every element you gave a **flag** is saved.

```lua
Lumen:SaveConfig("legit")        -- returns true, or false + error
Lumen:LoadConfig("legit")        -- returns true, or false + error
Lumen:ListConfigs()              -- { "legit", ... }
Lumen:DeleteConfig("legit")
Lumen:SetAutoload("legit")
Lumen:LoadAutoload()             -- call after building your UI
```

Files are stored in `<ConfigFolder>/settings/<name>.json`.

### Prebuilt config manager

One call builds a full config UI (create, load, overwrite, autoload, refresh):

```lua
local Settings = Window:CreateTab({ Name = "Settings" })
Lumen:BuildConfigSection(Settings)
```

## Flags and Lumen.Options

```lua
Main:CreateToggle({ Name = "ESP", CurrentValue = true }, "ESP")

print(Lumen.Options.ESP.CurrentValue)
Lumen.Options.ESP:Set(false)
```

Reading values: Toggle `.CurrentValue`, Slider `.CurrentValue`, Input `.CurrentValue`, Bind `.CurrentBind`, Dropdown `.CurrentOption`, ColorPicker `.Color`.

Use a **unique** flag for each element.

## Cleanup

